<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Nijhout (1990) & Brakefield et al. (1996) butterfly wing-vein focus determination and concentric French-flag eyespot ring morphogenesis (Bicyclus anynana & Junonia coenia (Nymphalidae: Satyrinae / Nymphalinae))",
        "Nijhout (1990) & Brakefield et al. (1996) butterfly wing-vein focus determination and concentric French-flag eyespot ring morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Bicyclus anynana & Junonia coenia (Nymphalidae: Satyrinae / Nymphalinae) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2001-nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bicyclus anynana & Junonia coenia (Nymphalidae: Satyrinae / Nymphalinae) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/HEAD/2001-nijhout-butterfly-eyespot-focus-rings.py> ;
    schema:about "Bicyclus anynana & Junonia coenia (Nymphalidae: Satyrinae / Nymphalinae)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "10. Stigmergy & Active Swarms" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Biofilm Wrinkles & Hex Combs" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Chemotactic / Stigmergic Pe" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Bicyclus" ;
